<title>UK: Bear Stearns details $1.28 bln Brazil MYDFA bond.</title>
<headline>Bear Stearns details $1.28 bln Brazil MYDFA bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lead manager Bear Stearns has detailed a $1.28 billion 144A bond offering, which is being launched on behalf of the Dart family.</p>
<p>The deal securitises all of Brazil's remaining multi-year deposit facility agreement (MYDFA) loans which were not restructured as Brady bonds.</p>
<p>The issue will be priced later today.</p>
<p> BORROWER   MYDFA TRUST</p>
<p> AMT    $1.28 BLN     SPREAD  ** 13/16     LEGAL MAT   15.SEP.07</p>
<p> ISS PRICE  **	  BASE	 6M LIBOR  AVE LIFE    6.19 YRS</p>
<p> NOTES   ** TO BE PRICED AT A DISCOUNT PRICE TO YILED 110-120</p>
<p>		B.P. OVER BRAZILIAN EI BONDS.</p>
<p>		GRADUATED AMORTISATION STRUCTURE.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8863</p>
